style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.5 M1 and YP 3.1.13 were =
released.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have two weeks before the =
3.5 M2 build.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The autobuilder has undergone =
significant changes. There are some not unexpected&nbsp; issues with the =
new distros now in use there such as python 3.12 deprecations which =
trigger warnings on Fedora 35. One of the workers does appear to have =
what is potentially a hardware issue and not all the workers have =
migrated to SSDs yet (about 50% so far) so there will be some further =
disruption as this takes place.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>On modern kernels, we now have =
the capability within bitbake to disable networking on a per task basis =
without extra user privileges. There is discussion on the mailing list =
on how we should enable this and whether it should be on an opt-in or =
opt-out basis. There is a proof of concept patchset for the opt-out =
basis and some good arguments for and against the opt-in =
approach.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The new year triggered some =
reproducible build failures in openssl and webkit due to changing =
copyright years in the source files, which is a sign of how detailed our =
reproducibility tests are.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There is a patchset =
implementing reproducibility for go which is a welcome improvement and =
much less invasive than previous approaches.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent issues continue to =
be at record high levels and help is very much welcome in trying to =
resolve them. You can see the list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to =
see by searching for the &#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l8 level1 =
